  "section": "9.17",
  "rulesText": "Some monsters are associated with curses, whether as part of their origins or due to their ability to spread curses - werewolves being a prime example.\n\nYou decide how a spell like Remove Curse affects a creature with accursed origins. For example, you might decide that a mummy was created through a curse and it can be destroyed permanently only by casting Remove Curse on its corpse.",
  "ruleCategory": "Curse"
}
